UID:f32ca95fa3d7341c@role-family-law.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260804T195436Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260804
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Kathleen M. Barron v. John D. Barron
DESCRIPTION:MAINE SUPREME JUDICIAL COURT Reporter of Decisions \nDecision:
  2026 ME 77 \nDocket: Pen-25-563 \nSubmitted \nOn Briefs: June 16\, 2026 \
 nDecided: August 4\, 2026 \n \nPanel: STANFILL\, C.J.\, and LAWRENCE\, DOU
 GLAS\, and TAUB\, JJ.\, and HORTON\, A.R.J.  \n \n \nKATHLEEN M. BARRON \n
  \nv. \n \nJOHN D. BARRON \n \n \nTAUB\, J. \n[¶1]  John D. Barron appeal
 s from a divorce judgment issued by the \nDistrict Court (Bangor\, Roberts
 \, A.R.J. ) dissolving his marriage to Kathleen M. \nBarron.  John contend
 s that the court erred in distributing marital property \nbecause it used 
 information from Kathleen’s 2022 financial statement instead \nof inform
 ation from her 2024 financial statement.\n1  We agree\, vacate the \njudgm
 ent in part\, and remand for further proceedings.  We also deny Kathleen
 ’s \nmotion for sanctions\, which argues that John’s appeal is frivolo
 us.   \n \n1  Because the parties share the same surname\, we refer to the
 m by their given names.   \n 2 \nI.  BACKGROUND \n[¶2]  Kathleen filed fo
 r divorce from John in 2022.  In 2022\, both Kathleen \nand John filed fin
 ancial statements as required by M.R. Civ.  P. 108(c).  On \nMay 15\, 2024
 \, prior to the final hearing on May  31\, 2024\, Kathleen filed an \nupda
 ted financial statement as required by M.R. Civ. P. 108(d)(4).  John did n
 ot \nfile an updated financial statement. \n[¶3]  At the final hearing\, 
 the only issue s were spousal support and the \ndivision of marital proper
 ty.  Kathleen entered her 2024 financial statement in \nevidence and testi
 fied as to its contents.  Kathleen also entered John’s \n2022 financial 
 statement in evidence.   Neither Kathleen’s 2022 financial \nstatement n
 or an updated financial statement from John were entered in \nevidence.   
 \n[¶4]  After the hearing\, the parties submitted proposed calculations f
 or \nthe division of their marital property.  In her proposed calculation\
 , Kathleen did \nnot use the information from her testimony or her 2024 fi
 nancial statement.  \nInstead\, she used both her and John’s 2022 financ
 ial statements and calculat\nhttps://www.courts.maine.gov/courts/sjc/lawco
 urt/2026/26me077.pdf
URL:https://www.courts.maine.gov/courts/sjc/lawcourt/2026/26me077.pdf
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:c5e9fc0a690bb4d0@role-family-law.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260804T143723Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260804
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] 8/4/2026: Maine eCourts Scheduled to be Imple
 mented in  Cumberland County Courts in September
DESCRIPTION:Home\nSkip to top navigation\nSkip to side navigation\nSkip to
  content\nSkip to footer\nMaine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp
 \n|\nSearch Maine.gov\nCOURT ALERTS IN EFFECT.\nSee Active Alerts\nHome\n
 →\nNews & Announcements\nMaine eCourts Scheduled to be Implemented in  C
 umberland County Courts in September\nDate:\n8/4/2026\nThe Maine Judicial 
 Branch announced today that the schedule for transitioning courts in Cumbe
 rland County (comprising Judicial Region 2) from paper filing to electroni
 c filing (eFiling) is scheduled for Monday\, September 28\, 2026. The next
  implementation includes all case types in the Cumberland County Unified C
 riminal Docket (UCD)\, Cumberland County Superior Court\, Portland Distric
 t Court\, and Bridgton District Court.\nAttorneys\, government agencies (e
 xcept law enforcement agencies)\, and parties who file more than six non-e
 mergency cases in a calendar year\, are required to eFile in courts that h
 ave implemented Maine eCourts. Self-represented parties are not required t
 o eFile and can continue to file documents as they always have\, in paper 
 at the courthouse\, by mail\, or by email if filing a protection from abus
 e or harassment case.\nAttorneys and other required eFilers should prepare
  in advance for the transition\, and take note of upcoming presentation an
 d trainings:\nPresentation for Cumberland County Legal Professionals and S
 takeholders\nThe Maine Judicial Branch will hold a virtual presentation by
  ZOOM on August 10th\, at noon to discuss the implementation of Maine eCou
 rts and electronic filing (eFiling) in Judicial Region 2\, Cumberland Coun
 ty Courts. Attorneys and other professional filers are encouraged to atten
 d.\nTopic: Maine eCourts in Region 2: Cumberland County\nDate & Time: Mond
 ay\, August 10\, 2026 at 12:00 p.m.\nPlease click the link below to join t
 he webinar:\nhttps://courts-maine-gov.zoom.us/j/94955753059\nPasscode: 993
 548\nThe webinar will be recorded and made available on the Judicial Branc
 h website on the Maine eCourts Training & Resources page followi\nhttps://
 www.courts.maine.gov/news/article.html?id=13357575
URL:https://www.courts.maine.gov/news/article.html?id=13357575
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
